        "headline": "A#-minor 143bpm dub-techno arc anchored on a Bb/A# tonic with a 5-minute breathing structure and a deep 28-second break before the final push",
        "diagnosis": "A# minor (Bb minor, 3A), NOT G minor as the detector claims. Tonic drone with i↔I major/minor flicker plus moves to bVI (F#) and iv (D#) — classic dub-techno modal stasis, the major/minor ambiguity doing the emotional work. Textbook long-form arc with a deep 28s breakdown at 3:22 before the climax. Sub-heavy balance (52% sub / 19% bass) = dub-techno mix philosophy, but mids likely under-represented in the master.",
